WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:02.400
In the battle to defend 
Filianno Castle...

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.560
...the key to victory was the young boy
the Princess summoned.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.400
The Hero has found out that
he cannot return to his world.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.740
He did so well on the battlefield.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.910
I'm sure the Hero is troubled.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.530
But, well at time like this!!

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.040
Ricotta Elmar always finds a solution!

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.850
The battle is over!!

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.190
Hooray, hooray!!

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.570
Both sides were not able 
to conquer the enemy,

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.830
I wanna go back!
But I can’t...? A hero in Flonyald

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.340
so the result was determined by the score...

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.740
...and it was the first victory 
for Biscotti in a long while!

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.640
We will call on the Loran,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.110
leader of the knights 
for the Biscotti Army...

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:20.280
...and ask him a little 
about this battle...

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.740
Loran, sir, how does that sound?

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.210
<i>Fine.</i>

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.710
<i>And sir?</i>

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.030
<i>If it's possible we'd like to speak with</i>

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:31.700
<i>the Hero who had a fabulous debut today.</i>

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.400
<i>Um, err.</i>

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.360
<i>The hero, we will reveal 
more about him later...</i>

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.500
<i>Today, we'll just...</i>

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.680
<i>Keep it a mystery? I see!</i>

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.690
<i>Well then we'll ask Rolan
to speak more instead!</i>

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:49.110
-Nice thinking, Rolan...

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:49.110
<i>-Thank you.</i>

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.570
Can't go home...
I can't go home from here...

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.360
We can't show our hero like this...

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:00.770
Oh, what shall we do?

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.950
I'm sure the Hero is worried.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.840
Phew, what should we do...

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.830
Still...

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.130
Princess, you have your 
own responsibilities.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.240
Oh, but Amelita...

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.260
After this you must give a message

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.130
of appreciation to the 
soldiers of both sides.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.560
You must greet Her Majesty Leo
about the ending of the battle...

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.770
...have the leader
of the winning country interview...

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.750
...give thanks to the groups
that sponsored the event...

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.640
Then you have the concert,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.770
which you can't have 
without a rehearsal...

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.840
So just for today, you 
will have to leave

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.660
this issue with the 
Hero up to the elders.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.620
I know...

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.280
And in these types of situations,
your old friend from school...

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.790
...Chief Elmar will do something!

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:54.540
I will find a way to return
the summoned hero to his world...

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.990
I am responsible because I didn't stop

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.030
the Princess from summoning the Hero...

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.650
...and I didn't confirm 
things properly...

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.220
I don't want to see
the Princess looking so sad!

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.200
I guess that makes sense...

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.120
This is a different world...

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.460
Really, you shouldn't have accepted

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.470
if you weren't ready 
for the consequences.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.870
Ready? I didn't have a choice! That dog!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.880
I was jumping from the landing and
he set up a pitfall!

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.090
Pitfall? Tatsumaki did that?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.090
Let's see...

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:56.470
Welcome to Flonyald, 
welcome to Biscotti...

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:03.610
Huh?

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.020
Caution: This is a hero summons.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:09.870
What?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.490
If you do not accept,
do not step on this seal...

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.280
How could I possibly read that!

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.420
I don't know! Don't tell me!

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:25.220
Well the elders are investigating
a way to get you home.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.140
I'm sure they'll find a way...

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.140
I hope so.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.440
Well anyway, in the meantime...

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:37.110
You are an idiot,
but you must be treated as a guest.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.650
You won't have any problems
with your life here.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.820
First things first, take this.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:43.530
What? Money?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.570
I can't accept that...

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.390
It's the reward
for your work on the battlefield.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.070
If you don't accept it

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.490
I'm sure there are many soldiers

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.840
that take part in the 
battles because it's fun...

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.160
...but the reward money 
is a way of telling

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.840
how much you contributed to the battle.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.370
And I suppose that the truth is

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:12.640
they want to win back 
the participation fee.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.060
Participation fee?

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:21.150
Oh gee, it looks like I have to
teach you everything, don't I?

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.460
Battles are a method for 
countries to interact...

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.630
...but at the same time 
they are an event run

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.340
by entire countries and organizations.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.990
We fought Galette this time,

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.100
...between villages and organizations,
like civil wars.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.790
You mean something like a competition

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.350
and festival between villages...

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.610
Well, I guess you can put it that way...

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.430
When a battle is planned, the planner

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:14.120
gathers participation fees 
from the participants...

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.170
...that is all allocated 
to each country.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:25.630
Then the battle is held,
and the winning country take 60%...

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.880
...and the losing country takes
the remaining 40%.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.470
That is the basic ratio determined
by the Continental Agreement.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:36.160
Of the divided cost, at least half goes

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.910
to the soldiers that participated...

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.400
The percentage is also determined
in the Agreement.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.990
And the remaining half is
the national profit from the battle.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:51.530
We use it to build 
hospitals, fortresses,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.530
and pay the people for 
work for the public.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.330
It is used to protect the country.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:03.980
And um, what about real wars...

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.540
when the Continental 
Agreement is not honored?

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.620
Wars where people actually die?

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.650
If we look back in history,

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.590
it's not like we've never 
had those kinds of wars...

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.600
Especially with demons...

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:21.680
The reason people don't get hurt in
our battles

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.470
is because of the Flonya power...

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:26.560
...protecting people from battle injuries
that lies in the land designated as battlefields.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:30.900
In other places you could get hurt
or even killed.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.870
So then how many places are protected?

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.710
Countries and cities... 
fortresses have been

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:39.370
built in areas where the 
protective power is strong.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.310
There are many dangerous areas
on the roads and on the countryside.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:44.390
Especially in the roads,

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:47.240
there is also a high risk 
of large wild animals.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.570
But, if you join a troop 
moving for battle,

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.130
I see!

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:59.640
But, seriously, you really  
don't know anything!

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.440
And so now we walk, let's 
head over to Rico's.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.150
You never know,
she might have figured something out.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.070
Uh, yeah.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:16.770
Excuse me, sir!
I, Ricotta Elmar...

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.110
...have wholeheartedly been searching

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:21.370
for a way to return 
our Hero to his world!

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:24.660
However, I have had no success yet.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.470
Hey Rico, calm down.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:29.840
We understand that it's going 
to take a while to find a way...

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:30.820
What?

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:32.980
But...

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.050
That's right... yup.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:37.840
Is that really so?

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.430
You were saying you had a deadline?

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:45.170
Umm, three days before
the end of spring break...

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:48.050
...the day before that 
I need to be home, so...

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.360
Another 16 days!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:51.550
16 days!

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.730
I'm starting to have hope again!

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:56.490
Good, I'm counting on you!

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.330
But before that...

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.370
<b>Outside the range</b>

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.370
If we were to go to the hole
I was summoned from...

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.690
...do you think I might get a signal?

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.240
Signal?

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:19.510
Umm, can't get through...

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.180
See, I told you so!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.020
Well you gotta try anyway!

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.770
Hero-sama!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.270
We are ready!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.360
Uh, what's that?

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.690
This machine strengthens and increases

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.990
the Flonya waves used for the broadcast.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.890
I invented this when 
I was 5 years old...

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:47.190
...and it's still being used
throughout the continent!

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:51.800
Well, Hero...

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.720
Uh, right...

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.170
<b>Outside the range</b>

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.890
I got a signal!!

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.220
Wow, Ricotta, you did it!

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:08.060
Thank you very much!
This is wonderful!

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.110
Okay! Well here I go!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.170
Hello?

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:41.600
I got through!

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.310
Congratulations!

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:46.250
Hello? Is it you, Sink?

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.030
You sound so far away...

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.900
Where are you?
The airport?

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.560
Yeah, something like that...

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.560
Oh, did you get my email?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.900
My dad can't come.
 He has to work.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.030
But Mom and I can join you on your trip!

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.080
Okay, that's great!

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:07.170
My mom is looking forward to
seeing the cherry blossoms.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:12.290
Sink, what's wrong? Are you feeling ok?

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:16.080
Huh? Why? I'm fine.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:17.610
If you say so...

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:22.210
Oh, and uh, my phone 
isn't working right,

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:26.990
so it might be hard to 
catch me for a while...

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.930
But I'm fine so don't worry...

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.670
Um, okay...

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.040
I won't worry.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.690
-Oh!
-Huh?

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.170
If you're gonna be hard to catch,

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:46.800
you should
contact your parents and Nanami-chan...

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.160
...they'll worry...

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:52.100
Uh, right, it's fine...

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.050
Bye now.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:00.670
Ricotta, Sorry...

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:03.070
Can I try again?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:05.330
There are some other 
people I need to contact.

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:07.790
Sure!

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:09.100
Oh! Hero-sama.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:13.290
Would you mind letting 
me see that device,

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.850
the phone as you call 
it... could I study it?

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:21.110
If I could just take it apart a little bit
and see how it's made!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.760
When I see a machine I'm 
not familiar with...

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.520
...the base of my tail and my burning

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.990
desire to research it start throbbing!

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.740
Don't worry. I can put back together.

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:34.790
If you take it apart,
the guarantee will become void!

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:38.090
That's fine. I guarantee it!

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.150
It's not that kind of guarantee,
it's the phone company's!!

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.380
I just want to touch it a little...

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:45.300
Umm... I see...

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.130
Has the Hero been able 
to contact his home?

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.720
Yes, he and Rico are both very relieved.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.890
The Hero has said that he wants to stay

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:59.890
positive and even take part 
in battle's while he is here.

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:00.910
I see,

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.490
I must let the Princess 
know immediately.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.140
-Yes, please let her know.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:06.920
-And..

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:07.830
Yes?

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.980
Lord Dalkian and Yukikaze will be

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.490
back from their journey 
today or tomorrow.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.180
Oh! That's good to hear!

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.410
Éclair, any good news?

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.670
Lord Dalkian is on his way home!

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.600
Is that so?

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.780
That means Yukki is coming home too?

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:24.560
Yes.

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:25.530
Who?

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.980
The strongest knight in Biscotti.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:30.970
Lord Dalkian and our 
dear friend, Yukikaze.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:34.110
They are both very impressive!

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:42.280
Oh, that's unusual...
It is the Tochigami-sama.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:43.730
Tochigami?

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:46.260
Hey, you really don't 
know anything, do you?

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.030
It is a creature that lives in the ground
and is like a spirit.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.710
When there's a Tochigami-sama, 
it's a sign

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.890
that the land is full 
of the gifts of nature.

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:56.080
Hmmm.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:59.080
Really?

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:03.670
Yes, our Hero is now enjoying the sights

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.510
with Ricotta and Eclair.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.090
He says he will come to the concert.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:09.520
I'm glad...

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:13.300
Is he getting along 
with Rico and Eclair?

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:16.310
As far as I can see,
they are getting on just fine.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:22.650
Well I can't relax yet,
but I'm relieved to hear that.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:27.030
Yes, dear Princess,
you have so much on your shoulders.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.650
I wouldn't be able to do it
without everyone's support...

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:32.620
I have to try and do what I can.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.290
Excuse me, captain of the knights,

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.000
Oh, right!

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:44.820
...I have to apologize to the Hero...

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:49.090
...and tell him he did
wonderfully on the battlefield...

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:53.310
...I wonder if it's alright
if I pat the Hero on the head...

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:55.300
I hope that won't be rude...

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.650
Oh, and I have to praise Eclair too!

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:04.190
And I have to do my 
best at the concert...

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:05.540
And...

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.970
Oh Leo-sama...

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:21.750
Back then,
you used to complement my singing so...

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:24.330
Why will you no longer hear me sing?

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:35.240
Leo-sama, do you not want to go to

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:39.020
Why should I?

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:41.340
I don't want to hear 
that Dog Princess sing.

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:44.180
I see...

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:47.770
well then, shall we run 
a bit of interference?

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.390
I couldn't do something 
so undignified...

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:52.280
...as a losing country interfering

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.490
in the winning country's celebration.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:58.830
Well then,
please enjoy your drinks tonight...

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:01.910
That's what I intend to do.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:02.590
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:04.410
By the way, what happened to Gaul?

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:06.980
He said he would be coming this way...

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:09.200
Of course, he did.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:14.930
My sister was defeated...

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:18.390
It seems so.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.390
His style is the same 
light armor warrior

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.970
type as you, Gaul-sama.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:23.590
Interesting.

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:26.270
It's not like
I'm getting revenge for my sister...

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.300
...but I guess we could
play around with him a bit.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:33.890
We don't want you to show up

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:35.990
at the Princess's concert 
all sweaty and smelly.

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:39.050
You should take a bath 
before the concert.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.380
A bath? Where is it?

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:45.280
There's a sign,
and you can ask someone inside.

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:51.670
But there's nobody here...

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:55.520
I guess they're all busy
getting ready for the concert...

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:57.470
...so where's the bath?

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:00.470
Oh, is that it?

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:09.560
Ah, lockers... Yes, I'm right!

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:11.560
Woohoo!

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:13.050
Spa     
Currently available for women

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:16.050
Millefiore is using.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.610
Whoaa! This is amazing!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.310
An outdoor bath!

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:30.120
Oh, is there some else here?

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:47.980
Uhh... Hero-sama?

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:05.370
Uhhh! I didn't see anything!!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.870
I'm, I'm sorry.
So disgraceful in front of our hero...

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:11.870
Um, I, I didn't think 
anyone else was here.

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:14.380
I didn't think the Princess would be here...
I, I'm so sorry!

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:17.380
Um, Hero-sama.

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:21.410
Sorry!

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:26.140
I, I usually can't come to
this large bath, so I...

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:27.940
I thought it would
be a good opportunity..

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:30.770
Uh, um! I'll go now!

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:33.280
Please, Hero-sama, take your time!

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:47.240
Um, Hero-sama?

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.590
Ye, yes!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.330
There's a lot I'd like to discuss with you,
about the summons...

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:56.290
...and about what we do from here on...

00:19:56.640 --> 00:20:01.890
So after the concert is over,
can we meet for a while?

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:04.300
Uh, yes, of course!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.760
Thank you!

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.560
Well then I'll see you later.

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.150
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:22.930
I should have asked the princess,

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:25.490
...this isn't the ladies bath, is it?

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:28.380
It can't be...

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:31.000
Princess?

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:45.050
We are from the Galette 
Lion Army Territory!

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.320
We are the Secret Intelligence Unit

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.930
Genoise!

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:55.480
Princess!!

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:56.310
Here!

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:58.350
Hero of Biscotti!

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:02.490
We have your precious Princess!

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:07.910
<i>We'll be waiting at the Mion Fortress!</i>

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.910
<i>Only an hour and half until 
it's time for the Princess</i>

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.600
<i>to sing at the concert.</i>

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.410
<i>Will you rescue her in time?</i>

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:18.540
<i>This means,
based on the Continental Agreement...</i>

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:22.460
<i>...we are holding a
"High-profile Abduction Recapture Battle".</i>

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:24.810
<i>Our forces are 200 men.</i>

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:27.260
<i>They are elite troops
under the direct command of Gaul-sama.</i>

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:32.010
<i>Gaul-sama wishes to have
a one-on-one battle with the Hero.</i>

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:34.420
<i>If the Hero does not 
accept the challenge,</i>

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:36.020
<i>we don't know what will 
happen to the Princess.</i>

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.520
<i>Of course I accept the challenge!</i>

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.630
I am Sink,
the hero of Biscotti

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:47.740
summoned by the Princess!

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:52.870
I will take on anyone who threatens her!

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:34.030
Gloooom...

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:35.780
Hero! {Might need a split here} Rico, you'll have to handle this one.

00:23:35.280 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>Charge! Princess Recovery Battle!!</b>

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:38.000
Roger that. I'll do my best again next time!

00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:39.830
Gloooom...
